0..75 Comment "//! A flow at a universe above the smallest: the codes it relates are large"
76..154 Comment "//! types, which pack a type in a field, so they live one level up and so does"
155..228 Comment "//! the flow between them. The classifier `Flow(Type[+, 1], A, B)` is the"
229..262 Comment "//! directed hom of that universe"
263..334 Comment "//! [Gratzer-2026-directed_univalence_simplicial_homotopy_type_theory],"
335..414 Comment "//! Definition 1.2. It stands at its level as `Path` stands at every level. The"
415..486 Comment "//! kernel replays each declaration here at its flow over the level-one"
487..562 Comment "//! universe. A transport or a ride along a path or a flow at that universe"
563..640 Comment "//! reads its motive\'s binder there too, so the motive\'s body decodes a large"
641..663 Comment "//! code at level one."
664..667 Comment "//!"
668..684 Comment "//! - see: #1628"
685..701 Comment "//! - see: #1837"
702..781 Comment "//! - cites: [Gratzer-2026-directed_univalence_simplicial_homotopy_type_theory]"
